* [[January 24]] – At least 70 people are killed and 10 others missing after [[2026 West Bandung landslide|major landslides]] in [[West Java]], Indonesia.<ref>{{Cite news|date=31 January 2026|title=Update Longsor Cisarua: 70 Kantong Jenazah Dievakuasi, 10 Masih Dicari|trans-title=Update death toll Cisarua landslide: 70 bodies have been found, 10 others still missing|url=https://www.cnnindonesia.com/nasional/20260131192802-20-1323204/update-longsor-cisarua-70-kantong-jenazah-dievakuasi-10-masih-dicari/|language=id|access-date=1 February 2026|publisher=CNN Indonesia}}</ref>
* [[January 25]] – [[2025–26 Myanmar general election]]: In an election widely considered as neither free nor fair, the pro-military [[Union Solidarity and Development Party]] wins a supermajority of seats in the [[Pyithu Hluttaw]] and the [[Amyotha Hluttaw]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Myanmar's military holds second phase of elections amid civil war |publisher=Al Jazeera |date=2026-01-11 |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/11/myanmars-military-holds-second-phase-of-elections-amid-civil-war |access-date=2026-01-26}}</ref>
* [[January 26]] – The body of [[Ran Gvili]], the last remaining Israeli hostage in the Gaza Strip, is recovered by the [[Israel Defense Forces|IDF]] from northern Gaza, thus ending the [[Gaza war hostage crisis]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://apnews.com/article/israel-gaza-hamas-rafah-26-1-2026-c0b373a26ef7f4524b9b2bdad766cfda|title=Israel recovers remains of the last hostage in Gaza. Ceasefire moves into tricky new phase|first1=Julia|last1=Frankel|first2=SAMY MAGDY Leer en|last2=español|date=January 26, 2026|website=AP News|access-date=March 7, 2026}}</ref>
* [[January 27]] – The [[India–European Union Free Trade Agreement]] is signed after nearly two decades of negotiations, eliminating [[Tariff|Tariffs]] on a broad range of products and services between the two regions.<ref>{{cite web |title=India and EU announce 'mother of all trade deals' |website=BBC News |date=27 January 2026 |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/crrnee01r9jo |access-date=27 January 2026}}</ref>
* [[January 28]] 
** [[Sarah Mullally]] becomes the first female [[Primate (bishop)|primate]] of the [[Church of England]] and [[Archbishop of Canterbury]].<ref>{{cite news |last=M |first=Muvija |date=28 January 2026 |title=First woman leader of the Church of England confirmed in ancient ceremony |url= https://www.reuters.com/world/uk/first-woman-leader-church-england-confirmed-ancient-ceremony-2026-01-28/ |access-date=28 January 2026 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
** [[2026 Rubaya mine collapse|Successive mine collapses]] at the [[Rubaya mines|Rubaya coltan mine]] in eastern [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]] kill more than 600 people.<ref>{{cite web | title=More than 200 killed in mine collapse in eastern DR Congo | publisher=Al Jazeera | date=2026-01-31 | url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/31/more-than-200-killed-in-mine-collapse-in-eastern-dr-congo-report | access-date=2026-02-01 | archive-date=February 2, 2026 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260202063227/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/31/more-than-200-killed-in-mine-collapse-in-eastern-dr-congo-report | url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[Storm Kristin]] causes a catastrophic impact in Portugal and Spain with €6 billion in damage in the central region of Portugal, 15 deaths and 2,000 injuries.<ref>{{cite web |title=Tempestade Kristin: quase dois meses depois, Hospital de Leiria continua a receber feridos por quedas de telhados |url=https://sicnoticias.pt/pais/2026-03-15-video-tempestade-kristin-quase-dois-meses-depois-hospital-de-leiria-continua-a-receber-feridos-por-quedas-de-telhados-882b1896 |website=Sic Noticias |access-date=26 March 2026 |archive-date=March 16, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260316120532/https://sicnoticias.pt/pais/2026-03-15-video-tempestade-kristin-quase-dois-meses-depois-hospital-de-leiria-continua-a-receber-feridos-por-quedas-de-telhados-882b1896 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Prejuízos das tempestades podem chegar aos seis mil milhões de euros |url=https://sicnoticias.pt/pais/2026-02-20-prejuizos-das-tempestades-podem-chegar-aos-seis-mil-milhoes-de-euros-9de16271 |website=Sic Noticias |access-date=26 March 2026 }}{{Dead link|date=July 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref>
* [[January 29]] 
** [[Ethiopian civil conflict (2018–present)|Ethiopian civil conflict]]: [[Ethiopia-TPLF clashes (2026–present)|Clashes]] erupt in the [[Tigray]] region in [[Ethiopia]] between [[Tigray Defense Forces|Tigrayan fighters]] and [[Ethiopian National Defense Force|Federal Forces]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Ethiopian Airlines cancels flights to Tigray as fears mount of renewed conflict|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cn40r3v770lo|publisher=[[BBC]]|date=29 January 2026|access-date=30 January 2026|last=Teferi|first=Michael}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=Clashes between government troops and Tigrayan forces erupt in Ethiopia|url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/1/29/clashes-between-government-troops-and-tigrayan-forces-erupt-in-ethiopia|publisher=[[Al Jazeera]]|access-date=30 January 2026|date=29 January 2026}}</ref>
** [[Insurgency in Balochistan]]: [[Jan–Feb 2026 Balochistan attacks|Fighting]] between the [[Balochistan Liberation Army]] and the [[Pakistan Armed Forces|Pakistani armed forces]] in several districts of [[Balochistan, Pakistan|Balochistan]], Pakistan, leaves at least 225 people dead.<ref>{{cite web |last=Zehri Shahid|first=Abdullah|title=Security forces kill 22 more terrorists in Balochistan, taking 48-hour total tally to 177|url=https://www.dawn.com/news/1970602/balochistan-residents-face-difficulties-as-mobile-internet-services-remain-suspended-for-3rd-day|website=Dawn|access-date=2 February 2026|language=en|date=2 February 2026}}</ref>
* [[January 30]] – Three million pages related to the [[Epstein files]] are released to the public, mentioning [[Prominent individuals mentioned in the Epstein files|many high-profile public figures]] worldwide.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-01-30 |title=Millions of Jeffrey Epstein files released by US justice department |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cevnmxyy4wjo |access-date=2026-02-05 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=February 5, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260205063839/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cevnmxyy4wjo |url-status=live }}</ref>

