[[File:Ilham Aliyev visited Iranian Embassy in Azerbaijan to offer condolences 5.jpg|thumb|Tribute to the [[Supreme Leader of Iran|Iranian Supreme Leader]], [[Ali Khamenei]] in the Iranian Embassy in [[Baku]], Azerbaijan following his [[Assassination of Ali Khamenei|assassination]] on February 28]]
* [[February 1]] – [[2026 Costa Rican general election]]: [[Laura Fernández Delgado]] is elected [[president of Costa Rica]], and [[Sovereign People's Party (Costa Rica)|her party]] additionally wins a majority in the [[Legislative Assembly of Costa Rica|Legislative Assembly]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mora |first=Carlos |date=2024-11-28 |title=TSE fija cronograma para elecciones nacionales de 2026 |url=https://crhoy.com/tse-fija-cronograma-para-elecciones-nacionales-de-2026/ |access-date=2025-10-26 |website=CR Hoy |language=es}}</ref>
* [[February 3]] – [[Boko Haram insurgency]]: [[Boko Haram]] [[2026 Kwara State attacks|attacks two villages]] in [[Kwara State]], Nigeria, killing at least 162 people.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-04 |title=Islamic militants kill at least 162 people in attacks on 2 villages in Nigeria, lawmaker says |url=https://apnews.com/article/nigeria-attack-katsina-security-north-057f3997877d7e2cf9e79dfcd596f868 |access-date=2026-02-08 |website=AP News |language=en |archive-date=February 4, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260204163846/https://apnews.com/article/nigeria-attack-katsina-security-north-057f3997877d7e2cf9e79dfcd596f868 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[February 5]] – The [[New START]] treaty [[Nuclear disarmament|limiting]] [[strategic nuclear weapon]]s between the [[United States]] and [[Russia]] expires.<ref>{{Cite web |title=As treaty expires, Russia says it's still ready to talk to US on nuclear limits|url=https://www.reuters.com/world/china/new-nuclear-age-beckons-clock-ticks-down-last-russia-us-arms-deal-2026-02-04/|last1=Antonov|first1=Dmitry|date=2026-02-04|access-date=2026-02-05|website=[[Reuters]]|last2=Trevelyan|first2=Mark}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=February 4, 2024 |title=New START to Expire in Two Years as Russia Refuses Talks |url=https://www.armscontrol.org/blog/2024-02/nuclear-disarmament-monitor |access-date=2024-11-18 |publisher=Arms Control Association}}</ref>
* [[February 6]]–[[February 22|22]] – The [[2026 Winter Olympics]] are held in [[Milan]] and [[Cortina d'Ampezzo]], Italy.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dreier |first=Frederick |date=2026-02-05 |title=We're Watching the 2026 Winter Olympics for These Thrilling Events |url=https://www.outsideonline.com/outdoor-adventure/snow-sports/cortina-winter-olympics-events/ |access-date=2026-02-06 |website=Outside |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |title=Milano Cortina 2026 Winter Olympic Games |url=https://www.britannica.com/event/Milano-Cortina-2026-Olympic-Winter-Games |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260204093738/https://www.britannica.com/event/Milano-Cortina-2026-Olympic-Winter-Games |archive-date=February 4, 2026 |access-date=2026-02-06 |work=Encyclopædia Britannica |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref>
