* [[February 8]]
** [[2026 Japanese general election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Sanae Takaichi]] wins a [[landslide victory]], securing a [[supermajority]] in the [[House of Representatives (Japan)|House of Representatives]].<ref>{{cite news |first1=Tamiyuki |last1=Kihara |first2=Yoshifumi |last2=Takemoto |first3=John |last3=Geddie |date=14 January 2026 |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/japan-pm-takaichi-mulls-feb-8-snap-election-yomiuri-reports-2026-01-13/ |title=Japan PM readies snap election, February 8 ballot eyed |language=en |publisher=Reuters |location=Tokyo |access-date=14 January 2026 |archive-date=January 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260114190939/https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/japan-pm-takaichi-mulls-feb-8-snap-election-yomiuri-reports-2026-01-13/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[2026 Thai general election]] and [[2026 Thai constitutional referendum|constitutional referendum]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Anutin Charnvirakul]] wins a plurality in the [[House of Representatives (Thailand)|House of Representatives]], and the [[Referendum]] to begin drafting a new [[Constitution of Thailand|constitution]] passes.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Tanakasempipat |first=Patpicha |date=2025-12-11 |title=Thailand Heads for Election as PM Set to Dissolve Parliament |url=https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-12-11/thai-pm-plans-to-dissolve-parliament-to-pave-way-for-early-vote |access-date=2025-12-11 |publisher=Bloomberg L.P. |language=en}}</ref>
** [[2026 Portuguese presidential election]]: [[Socialist Party (Portugal)|Socialist]] candidate [[António José Seguro]] is elected [[President of Portugal]] in the second round, beating [[Chega]] leader [[André Ventura]].<ref>{{Cite web|last1=Khalip |first1=Andrei |last2=Goncalves |first2=Sergio |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/portugal-votes-presidential-runoff-with-socialist-poised-victory-2026-02-08/|title=Portugal elects Socialist as president by landslide|work=Reuters |date=February 8, 2026 |access-date=March 7, 2026}}</ref>
* [[February 10]] – At least nine people, including the perpetrator, are killed, and 27 are injured in a [[2026 Tumbler Ridge shooting|mass shooting]] at [[Tumbler Ridge Secondary School]] and at a residence in [[Tumbler Ridge]], [[British Columbia]], Canada.<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Regalado |first1=Francesca |last2=Isai |first2=Vjosa |last3=Zhuang |first3=Yan |date=2026-02-11 |title=9 Killed and 25 Injured in Shootings in Tumbler Ridge, Canada |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/11/world/canada/canada-shooting-tumbler-ridge-british-columbia.html |access-date=2026-02-11 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-11 |title=Canada shooting latest: Nine killed and 25 injured in shootings at school and home in Tumbler Ridge |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/cr5lnzqdr5pt |access-date=2026-02-11 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=February 11, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260211025800/https://www.bbc.com/news/live/cr5lnzqdr5pt |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[February 11]] – [[2026 Barbadian general election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Mia Mottley]] wins every seat in the [[House of Assembly of Barbados|House of Assembly]] in a landslide victory.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/feb/11/mia-amor-mottley-on-course-for-third-term-as-barbados-heads-to-the-polls|title=Mia Amor Mottley on course for third term, as Barbados heads to the polls|first1=Natricia|last1=Duncan|first2=Colville|last2=Mounsey|date=February 11, 2026|access-date=March 7, 2026|work=The Guardian}}</ref>
* [[February 12]] – [[2026 Bangladeshi general election]] and [[2026 Bangladeshi constitutional referendum|constitutional referendum]]: The [[Bangladesh Nationalist Party]] led by [[Tarique Rahman]] wins a supermajority in the [[Jatiya Sangsad]], and the referendum on the [[July Charter]] passes.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Alam |first1=Julhas |last2=Saaliq |first2=Sheikh |last3=español |first3=SHONAL GANGULY Leer en |date=2026-02-12 |title=Bangladesh votes in its first election since the 2024 Gen Z uprising that ousted Hasina |url=https://apnews.com/article/bangladesh-election-hasina-bnp-3662258dc5c44535c839e7bcc4baed43 |access-date=2026-02-12 |website=AP News |language=en}}</ref>
* [[February 13]]–[[February 15|15]] – The [[62nd Munich Security Conference]] is held.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://securityconference.org/en/|title=Munich Security Conference|website=securityconference.org|access-date=January 17, 2026|archive-date=February 14, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250214013352/https://securityconference.org/en/|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[February 17]] – [[President of Peru]] [[José Jerí]] is [[Censure of José Jerí|censured]] by the [[Congress of the Republic of Peru|Congress of Peru]], removing him from office. He is succeeded by [[José María Balcázar]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-17 |title=Peru's leader José Jerí ousted over 'Chifa-gate' scandal, as presidential 'curse' strikes again |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/17/americas/peru-president-jose-jeri-ousted-intl-latam |access-date=2026-02-17 |publisher=CNN |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Elliott |first1=Lucinda |last2=Siniawski |first2=Natalia |title=Peru installs Jose Balcazar as interim president after Jeri ousted in political upheaval |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/peru-congress-elects-jose-balcazar-new-interim-president-2026-02-19/ |access-date=19 February 2026 |work=Reuters |date=19 February 2026}}</ref>
* [[February 16]]–[[February 21|21]] – The [[India AI Impact Summit 2026|AI Impact Summit]] takes place in [[New Delhi]], India.<ref>{{Cite web |title=AI Impact Summit Declaration, New Delhi (February 18 - 19, 2026) |url=https://www.mea.gov.in/bilateral-documents.htm?dtl/40809 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260223151649/https://www.mea.gov.in/bilateral-documents.htm?dtl/40809 |archive-date=February 23, 2026 |access-date=2026-02-27 |website=mea.gov.in |date=21 February 2026 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[February 22]]
** [[Kim Jong Un]] is re-elected as the [[General Secretary of the Workers' Party of Korea]] at the [[9th Congress of the Workers' Party of Korea|9th National Congress]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg18588mdko|title=Kim Jong Un re-appointed leader of North Korea's ruling party|date=23 February 2026|access-date=23 February 2026|last1=Koh|first1=Ewe|work=BBC News}}</ref>
** The [[2026 Laotian parliamentary election]] is held.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Lao PDR Sets February 22, 2026, for National and Provincial Elections |url=https://kpl.gov.la/detail.aspx?id=95854 |access-date=2025-12-10 |website=KPL |language=en-US}}</ref>
** [[2026 Jalisco operation]]: A military operation in [[Tapalpa]], [[Jalisco]], Mexico, kills 62 people including [[Jalisco New Generation Cartel]] leader [[El Mencho]].<ref>{{Cite web |last1=McCluskey |first1=Mitchell |date=2026-02-22 |title=Mexico's most-wanted drug leader 'El Mencho' killed in military operation as violent clashes erupt across country |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/22/americas/mexico-kill-drug-mencho-latam-intl |access-date=2026-02-22 |publisher=CNN |language=en|last2=Gutierrez|first2=Fidel}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Nicas |first1=Jack |last2=Wagner |first2=James |date=2026-02-23 |title=Operation That Killed Cartel Boss 'El Mencho' Left Dozens Dead, Officials Say: Live Updates |url=https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/02/23/world/mexico-cartel-el-mencho |access-date=2026-02-23 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>
* [[February 23]] – [[2025–2026 Dutch cabinet formation]]: [[Rob Jetten]] is sworn in as [[Prime Minister of the Netherlands]], heading a [[Jetten cabinet|minority government]].<ref>{{cite web | last=Corder | first=Mike | title=Netherlands' coalition government takes office led by youngest-ever premier Rob Jetten | website=AP News | date=2026-02-23 | url=https://apnews.com/article/netherlands-new-government-hague-jetten-524182c2237409d249e263248cd57d35 | access-date=2026-02-27}}</ref>
* [[February 26]] – [[2026 Afghanistan–Pakistan war]]: The government of [[Pakistan]] declares "open war" against the [[Taliban]] in [[Afghanistan]].<ref>{{cite web | last=Sprothen | first=Vera | title=Angriffe in Kabul: Pakistan erklärt Taliban-Regierung "offenen Krieg" | website=DIE ZEIT | date=2026-02-27 | url=https://www.zeit.de/politik/ausland/2026-02/afghanistan-pakistan-konflikt-angriffe-grenzregion-taliban-gxe | language=de | access-date=2026-02-27 | archive-date=February 27, 2026 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260227112215/https://www.zeit.de/politik/ausland/2026-02/afghanistan-pakistan-konflikt-angriffe-grenzregion-taliban-gxe | url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[February 27]] – [[2026 Zona da Mata floods]]: Floods and landslides in the [[Zona da Mata (Minas Gerais)|Zona da Mata]] region of [[Minas Gerais]], Brazil leave at least 70 people dead and thousands of others displaced.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://g1.globo.com/mg/minas-gerais/noticia/2026/02/25/chuvas-na-zona-da-mata-deixam-mais-de-30-mortos-e-dezenas-de-desaparecidos-dizem-bombeiros.ghtml|title=Chuvas na Zona da Mata deixam 70 mortos e 4 desaparecidos|last1=Ferreira|first1=Ana Carolina|last2=Jardim|first2=Paula|website=G1|date=28 February 2026|access-date=28 February 2026|language=pt-br}}</ref>
* [[February 28]] – [[2026 Iran war]]: Israel and the United States launch attacks on Iran, [[List of Iranian officials killed during the 2026 Iran war|killing many high-profile officials]], including Supreme Leader [[Ali Khamenei]].<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn5ge95q6y7t |title=US and Israel carry out joint attack on Iran as Tehran launches retaliatory strikes |date=28 February 2026 |work=BBC News |access-date=28 February 2026 |archive-date=February 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260228081423/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cn5ge95q6y7t |url-status=live }}</ref> Iran launches retaliatory strikes against Israel, as well as against US military bases in the [[Persian Gulf]],<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/feb/28/israel-attacks-iran-as-blasts-heard-in-tehran-live-updates?page=with:block-69a2c4c98f08e575db5bd4de#block-69a2c4c98f08e575db5bd4de|title=US and Israel attack Iran as Trump says 'major combat operations' under way – live |date=28 February 2026 |work=The Guardian |access-date=28 February 2026}}</ref> and [[2026 Strait of Hormuz crisis|closes the Strait of Hormuz]] by attacking vessels that try to pass.<ref>{{cite web | last=Butler | first=Gavin | title=Iran war: What is the Strait of Hormuz and why does it matter? | website=BBC Home | date=2025-06-23 | url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c78n6p09pzno | access-date=2026-03-24 | archive-date=March 4, 2026 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260304083124/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c78n6p09pzno | url-status=live }}</ref>

