* [[March 1]] – [[Abiemnom massacre]]: At least 169 people are killed and 50 injured when armed youth from [[Unity State]] attack [[Abiemnom County]] in [[South Sudan]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Nearly 170 killed, 50 injured in armed youth attack on South Sudan county |website=Anadolu Ajansı |date=2026-03-02 |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/africa/nearly-170-killed-50-injured-in-armed-youth-attack-on-south-sudan-county/3846437 |access-date=2026-03-02}}</ref>
* [[March 2]] – [[2026 Lebanon war]]: [[Hezbollah]] begins launching strikes against Israel in retaliation for the assassination of [[Supreme Leader of Iran|Iranian Supreme Leader]] [[Ali Khamenei]].<ref>{{Cite web|date=2 March 2026|title=Hezbollah Claims Rocket, Drone Strike On Israeli Missile Defence Site Near Haifa|url=https://www.bernama.com/en/news.php/?id=2529362|access-date=3 March 2026|agency=[[Bernama]]|archive-date=March 9, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260309060105/https://www.bernama.com/en/news.php/?id=2529362|url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=3 March 2026 |title=Hezbollah says targeted 3 Israeli bases after strikes on Lebanon |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260303-hezbollah-says-targeted-3-israeli-bases-after-strikes-on-lebanon|access-date=3 March 2026 |agency=[[Agence France-Presse]]|publisher=France 24}}</ref>
* [[March 4]] – [[2026 Iran war]]: The United States nuclear submarine {{USS|Charlotte|SSN-766|6}} [[Sinking of IRIS Dena|sinks]] the Iranian warship [[IRIS Dena|IRIS ''Dena'']] in the [[Indian Ocean]], off [[Sri Lanka]] with a torpedo, resulting in 140 sailors missing.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/c62gg44d53xt?post=asset%3A607bbc27-c19c-441c-9f02-522ce39f2c6b#post|title=US sinks Iranian warship with torpedo in Indian Ocean - Hegseth|date=4 March 2026 |work=BBC News|access-date=4 March 2026}}</ref>
* [[March 5]] – [[2026 Nepalese general election]]: The [[Rastriya Swatantra Party]] led by [[Balen Shah]] wins a landslide victory.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-09-16 |title=EC begins preliminary preparations for March elections |url=https://thehimalayantimes.com/nepal/ec-begins-preliminary-preparations-for-march-elections |access-date=2026-03-02 |website=The Himalayan Times |language=en}}</ref>
* [[March 5]]–[[March 17|17]] – The [[2026 World Baseball Classic]] is held in [[Japan]] and the [[United States]].<ref>{{cite news |date=March 21, 2023 |title=Classic will return in 2026, Commissioner confirms |url=https://www.mlb.com/world-baseball-classic/news/world-baseball-classic-will-return-in-2026 |publisher=Major League Baseball |access-date=December 24, 2023 |archive-date=March 22, 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230322101427/https://www.mlb.com/world-baseball-classic/news/world-baseball-classic-will-return-in-2026 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[March 6]]–[[March 15|15]] – The [[2026 Winter Paralympics]] are held in Milan and Cortina d'Ampezzo, Italy.<ref>{{cite web |last=Faulkner |first=Ruth |title=Milano Cortina 2026 Paralympic Winter Games open with stunning ceremony |url=https://www.paralympic.org/news/milano-cortina-2026-opening-ceremony |publisher=International Paralympic Committee |access-date=10 March 2026 |date=6 March 2026 |archive-date=March 6, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260306233506/https://www.paralympic.org/news/milano-cortina-2026-opening-ceremony |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[March 6]]–[[March 7|7]] – [[2026 Kenya floods]]: At least 66 people are killed after floods across [[Kenya]].<ref name="KTN YouTube" >{{cite web|url=https://m.youtube.com/watch?v=sT_6EbqFhMA|title=Kenya Flood Disaster: 66 dead as heavy rains wreak havoc in Nairobi|website=YouTube|publisher= KTN News|date=15 March 2026|type=video|access-date=15 March 2026}}</ref>
* [[March 8]] 
** [[2026 Iranian supreme leader election]]: [[Mojtaba Khamenei]], the son of [[Ali Khamenei]], is selected as the third [[Supreme Leader of Iran]].<ref>{{#invoke:Cite|web |date=9 March 2026 |title=Iranian Council of Experts Elects Mojtaba Khamenei as New Supreme Leader|url=https://easternherald.com/2026/03/09/mojtaba-khamenei-elected-iran-supreme-leader/|access-date=9 March 2026 |website=The Eastern Herald}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Tondo |first=Lorenzo |date=8 March 2026 |title=Ali Khamenei's son Mojtaba chosen as Iran's new supreme leader |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/08/ali-khameneis-son-mojtaba-chosen-as-irans-new-supreme-leader |access-date=8 March 2026 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077 |archive-date=March 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260308223046/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/08/ali-khameneis-son-mojtaba-chosen-as-irans-new-supreme-leader |url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[2026 Colombian parliamentary election]]: President [[Gustavo Petro]]'s party [[Historic Pact]] wins a plurality of seats in the [[Chamber of Representatives of Colombia|Chamber of Representatives]] and the [[Senate of Colombia|Senate]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-03-06 |title=Así quedó el calendario para las elecciones del 2026: fechas clave |url=https://www.eluniversal.com.co/colombia/2025/03/06/asi-quedo-el-calendario-para-las-elecciones-del-2026-fechas-clave/ |access-date=2025-11-08 |website=El Universal |language=es}}</ref>
** [[India national cricket team|India]] beats [[New Zealand national cricket team|New Zealand]] in the [[2026 Men's T20 World Cup]] final and secures its third title.<ref>{{Cite web |title=T20 World Cup final: India thrash New Zealand to make history with third title and first for any team on home turf |url=https://www.skysports.com/cricket/news/12123/13516965/t20-world-cup-final-india-thrash-new-zealand-to-make-history-with-third-title-and-first-for-any-team-on-home-turf |access-date=2026-03-08 |website=Sky Sports |language=en |archive-date=March 11, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260311115423/https://www.skysports.com/cricket/news/12123/13516965/t20-world-cup-final-india-thrash-new-zealand-to-make-history-with-third-title-and-first-for-any-team-on-home-turf |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[March 13]] 
** [[2026 Iran war]]: The [[United States Air Force]] conducts a large bombing [[2026 Kharg Island raid|raid on Kharg Island]], a key oil export hub off the [[Persian Gulf]] coast of Iran.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-03-11 |title=Without this small island, Iran's regime would have 'no income whatsoever' |url=https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-12/donald-trump-and-iran-oil-could-involve-kharg-island/106429772 |access-date=2026-03-21 |work=ABC News |language=en-AU |archive-date=March 12, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260312090843/https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-03-12/donald-trump-and-iran-oil-could-involve-kharg-island/106429772 |url-status=live }}</ref> 
** [[First Secretary of the Communist Party of Cuba]] [[Miguel Díaz-Canel]] confirms that Cuba is in talks with the [[Second presidency of Donald Trump|Trump administration]] to find solutions to the [[United States embargo against Cuba|oil blockade]] in the country.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-03-13 |title=Cuba confirms negotiations with US as country faces effects of oil blockade |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy8zv9gp0go |access-date=2026-03-14 |website=BBC |language=en-GB |archive-date=March 22, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260322023726/https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cwy8zv9gp0go |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[March 15]] 
** [[2026 Kazakh constitutional referendum]]: The new Constitution of [[Kazakhstan]] is accepted with 90% in favor.<ref>{{Cite web |date=11 September 2025 |title=President of Kazakhstan calls for drastic parliamentary reform including abolition of Senate |url=https://www.commonspace.eu/news/president-kazakhstan-calls-drastic-parliamentary-reform-including-abolition-senate |access-date=11 February 2026 |website=commonspace.eu |language=en}}</ref> 
** [[2026 North Korean parliamentary election]]: [[General Secretary of the Workers' Party of Korea|General Secretary]] [[Kim Jong Un]]'s [[Workers' Party of Korea|Workers' Party]] wins a landslide majority in the [[Supreme People's Assembly]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Park |first=Boram |date=4 March 2026 |title=N. Korea to elect representatives to Supreme People's Assembly this month following key party congress |url=https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20260304000851315?section=nk/nk |website=[[Yonhap News Agency]]|access-date=6 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-03-03 |title=N. Korea to elect representatives to Supreme People's Assembly this month following key party congress |url=https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/foreignaffairs/northkorea/20260304/n-korea-to-elect-representatives-to-supreme-peoples-assembly-this-month-following-key-party-congress |access-date=2026-03-06 |website=The Korea Times |language=en}}</ref>
** [[2026 Vietnamese legislative election]]: The [[Communist Party of Vietnam|Communist Party]] led by General Secretary [[Tô Lâm]] wins almost all the seats in the [[National Assembly of Vietnam]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://vietnamnews.vn/politics-laws/1718049/na-approves-shortened-term-sets-2026-election-date.html|title=NA approves shortened term, sets 2026 election date|website=Viet Nam News|date=21 May 2025}}</ref>
** [[2026 Republic of the Congo presidential election]]: Incumbent President [[Denis Sassou Nguesso]] wins reelection in a landslide victory.<ref>{{Cite news |date=31 December 2025 |title=Congo president Sassou Nguesso to seek re-election in March 2026 |publisher=[[France 24]] |url=https://www.france24.com/en/africa/20251230-congo-president-sassou-nguesso-seeks-re-election-2026}}</ref>
* [[March 16]] – [[2026 Kabul hospital airstrike]]: At least 400 people are killed and more than 250 injured in Pakistani airstrikes on a hospital in [[Kabul]], Afghanistan.<ref>{{Cite news |date=17 March 2026 |title=From sponsor to enemy: What's behind Pakistan's attack on Afghan Taliban? |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/sponsor-enemy-whats-behind-pakistans-attack-afghan-taliban-2026-03-17/ |access-date=17 March 2026 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[March 17]] – [[2026 Iran war]]: [[Ali Larijani]], the [[Secretary of the Supreme National Security Council]], is [[Assassination of Ali Larijani|assassinated]] by an Israeli airstrike.<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 March 2026 |title=Number one target: How Israel assassinated Iran's 'de-facto leader' Larijani |url=https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-890273 |access-date=18 March 2026 |website=The Jerusalem Post |language=en}}</ref>
* [[March 20]]{{ndash}}[[March 22|22]] {{ndash}} The [[2026 World Athletics Indoor Championships]] are held at [[Kujawsko-Pomorska Arena Toruń]] in [[Toruń]], [[BiT City]], [[Kuyavian–Pomeranian Voivodeship]], Poland.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Więcławski |first=Tomasz |date=23 March 2023 |title=Mamy to! Lekkoatletyczne Halowe Mistrzostwa Świata 2026 odbędą się w Toruniu |url=https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/news%2C1551846%2Cmamy-lekkoatletyczne-halowe-mistrzostwa-swiata-2026-odbeda-sie-w-toruniu |access-date=1 April 2023 |publisher=[[Polish Press Agency]] |language=Polish |archive-date=December 19, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251219060642/https://www.pap.pl/aktualnosci/news,1551846,mamy-lekkoatletyczne-halowe-mistrzostwa-swiata-2026-odbeda-sie-w-toruniu |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Czołgowski |first=Dariusz |date=22 March 2023 |title=Halowe mistrzostwa świata w lekkiej atletyce w 2026 r. odbędą się w Toruniu |url=https://torun.wyborcza.pl/torun/7,48723,29588155,halowe-mistrzostwa-swiata-w-lekkiej-atletyce-w-2026-r-odbeda.html |url-access=subscription |access-date=1 April 2023 |website=[[Gazeta Wyborcza]] |archive-date=May 29, 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240529153129/https://torun.wyborcza.pl/torun/7,48723,29588155,halowe-mistrzostwa-swiata-w-lekkiej-atletyce-w-2026-r-odbeda.html |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[March 22]] – [[2026 Slovenian parliamentary election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Robert Golob]] wins a plurality of seats in the [[National Assembly (Slovenia)|National Assembly]].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Slovenia's liberals and populists neck and neck, preliminary results show |url=https://apnews.com/article/slovenia-election-liberals-populists-6e24d78054ea2c3072c9b79b80ddd586 |date=22 March 2026 |access-date=22 March 2026 |work=AP |last=Zerdin |first=Ali |url-status=bot: unknown |archive-date=March 23, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260323063953/https://apnews.com/article/slovenia-election-liberals-populists-6e24d78054ea2c3072c9b79b80ddd586 |quote=The result means that none of the main parties will have a majority in the 90-member parliament and that whoever will form a future government will depend on smaller parties that will act as kingmakers. }}</ref>
* [[March 22]]–[[March 23|23]] – [[2026 Italian constitutional referendum]]: With a higher-than-expected turnout, voters reject a government-backed constitutional reform that would have separated the career paths of judges and prosecutors and split the [[High Council of the Judiciary (Italy)|High Council of the Judiciary]] into two bodies.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Giuffrida |first=Angela |date=2026-03-23 |title=Italian voters reject Giorgia Meloni's plan to overhaul judiciary |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/23/italy-voters-reject-overhaul-judiciary-giorgia-meloni |access-date=2026-03-31 |work=The Guardian |language=en-GB |issn=0261-3077}}</ref>
* [[March 23]] – A Lockheed C-130 of the [[Colombian Aerospace Force]] [[2026 Colombian Air Force Lockheed C-130 crash|crashes]] near [[Puerto Leguízamo]], Colombia, killing 69 people.<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 April 2026 |title=Rueda de Prensa 23 de abril de 2026 |url=https://www.fac.mil.co/es/noticias/rueda-de-prensa-23-de-abril-de-2026 |access-date=17 June 2026 |website=Fuerza Aeroespacial Colombiana |language=es}}</ref>
* [[March 24]]
** [[OpenAI]] announces that their flagship [[Sora (text-to-video model)|Sora]] app and [[API]] are shutting down.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jin |first=Berber |date=2026-03-24 |title=OpenAI Set to Discontinue Sora Video Platform App |url=https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/openai-set-to-discontinue-sora-video-platform-app-a82a9e4e |access-date=2026-03-24 |website=The Wall Street Journal |language=en-US |archive-date=March 25, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260325003359/https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/openai-set-to-discontinue-sora-video-platform-app-a82a9e4e |url-status=live }}</ref> The app is shut down on April 26, and its API shut down on September 24.<ref name="OpenAI-2026">{{Cite web |title=What to know about the Sora discontinuation |url=https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001152-what-to-know-about-the-sora-discontinuation |access-date=2026-03-28 |website=OpenAI Help Center |language=en-US}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Deprecations {{!}} OpenAI API |url=https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/deprecations |access-date=September 26, 2026 |website=OpenAI Developers |language=en}}</ref>
** [[2026 Danish general election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Mette Frederiksen]]'s coalition loses its majority in the [[Folketing]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-26 |title=Mette Frederiksen udskriver folketingsvalg |url=https://nyheder.tv2.dk/politik/2026-02-26-mette-frederiksen-udskriver-folketingsvalg |access-date=2026-02-26 |website=nyheder.tv2.dk |language=da-DK}}</ref>
** [[2026 Iran war]]: Iran's [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Iran)|Ministry of Foreign Affairs]] addresses in a letter to the [[United Nations]] that ships not tied to either the [[United States]] or [[Israel]] can pass through the [[Strait of Hormuz]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Eavis |first=Peter |date=2026-03-25 |title=Iran Says 'Non-Hostile' Ships Can Sail Through the Strait of Hormuz |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/24/world/middleeast/iran-strait-of-hormuz-ships.html |access-date=2026-03-25 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

=== April ===
[[File:Earthset (art002e009288).jpg|thumb|''[[Earthset]]'' photo taken on April 6 during [[Artemis II]]'s lunar flyby]]
[[File:8 April 2026 Isreali attacks on Beirut (2).jpg|thumb|Aftermath of the [[8 April 2026 Israeli attacks on Lebanon|April 8 Israeli attacks]] in Beirut, Lebanon]]
* [[April 1]] – [[NASA]] launches the [[Artemis II]] [[Flyby (spaceflight)|lunar flyby]] mission, marking the first crewed flight beyond [[low Earth orbit]] since [[Apollo 17]] in 1972.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Low |first=Lauren E. |date=2026-04-01 |title=Liftoff! NASA Launches Astronauts on Historic Artemis Moon Mission |url=https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/liftoff-nasa-launches-astronauts-on-historic-artemis-moon-mission/ |access-date=2026-04-01 |website=NASA |archive-date=May 7, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260507230901/https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/liftoff-nasa-launches-astronauts-on-historic-artemis-moon-mission/ |url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[April 6]] – The crew of Artemis II breaks the record for the furthest humans have ever been from Earth, reaching a maximum distance of 252,756 miles (406,771&nbsp;km) as they travel around the [[far side of the Moon]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-06 |title=Artemis astronauts travel further from Earth than any humans before - watch live |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/clyr8k06jv7t |access-date=2026-04-06 |website=[[BBC News]] |archive-date=April 19, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260419171754/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/clyr8k06jv7t |url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[April 7]] 
** [[2026 Vietnamese presidential election]]: The [[National Assembly of Vietnam]] elects General Secretary [[Tô Lâm]] as the new [[president of Vietnam]], replacing [[Lương Cường]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://english.news.cn/20260407/ed18537e45de4a1dabae914f80d5a145/c.html |title=Vietnamese party chief elected state president |publisher=Xinhua |work=english.news.cn |date=7 April 2026 |access-date=7 April 2026 |archive-date=April 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260408231951/https://english.news.cn/20260407/ed18537e45de4a1dabae914f80d5a145/c.html |url-status=live}}</ref>
** [[2026 Iran war]]: Following an ultimatum from Trump regarding the [[Strait of Hormuz]], the United States and Iran agree on a [[2026 Iran war ceasefire|two-week ceasefire]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-07 |title=Trump agrees to two-week ceasefire if Iran opens Strait of Hormuz - follow live |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c5yw4g3z7qgt |access-date=2026-04-07 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB |archive-date=April 8, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260408030438/https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c5yw4g3z7qgt |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[April 8]] – [[Israel]] launches a series of [[8 April 2026 Lebanon attacks|airstrikes across Lebanon]], targeting [[Hezbollah]] infrastructure. More than 300 people are killed and over 1,100 injured.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Israeli military launches largest strikes against Hezbollah in Lebanon |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/israeli-military-launches-largest-strikes-against-hezbollah-lebanon-2026-04-08/ |date=2026-04-08 |access-date=2026-04-09 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[April 10]]
** [[2026 Djiboutian presidential election]]: Incumbent President [[Ismaïl Omar Guelleh]] is re-elected for a sixth term.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Djibouti president re-election confirmed with 97% of vote |url=https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260421-djibouti-president-re-election-confirmed-with-97-of-vote |date=21 April 2026 |access-date=23 April 2026 |work=France24}}</ref>
** The crew of Artemis II successfully returns to Earth, splashing down safely in the [[Pacific Ocean]] near [[San Diego]], [[California]], United States. The four crew members are extracted from the capsule and taken by helicopter to the [[USS John P. Murtha|USS ''John P. Murtha'']].<ref>{{Cite news |title=Artemis crew home safely after completing historic mission to the Moon |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr51z54d5rpo |work=BBC News |date=11 April 2026 |access-date=11 April 2026 |archive-date=April 11, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260411113739/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr51z54d5rpo |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[April 11]] – [[2026 Iraqi presidential election]]: The Iraqi Parliament elects [[Nizar Amidi]] of the [[Patriotic Union of Kurdistan]] (PUK) as the new [[President of Iraq]], winning with 227 votes in the second round.<ref>{{cite news |title=PUK's Nizar Amedi elected Iraqi president in session boycotted by KDP |url=https://www.rudaw.net/english/middleeast/iraq/110420261 |work=Rudaw |date=11 April 2026 |access-date=16 April 2026}}</ref>
* [[April 12]]
** [[2026 Hungarian parliamentary election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Viktor Orbán]] loses re-election in a landslide to [[Péter Magyar]]'s [[Tisza Party]], ending 16 years of [[Fidesz–KDNP]] rule.<ref>{{cite web |last1=Seddon |first1=Sean |last2=Adler |first2=Katya |last3=Thorpe |first3=Nick |last4=Kirby |first4=Paul |last5=Palfi |first5=Rita |last6=Vaidyanathan |first6=Rajini |title=Viktor Orbán ousted after 16 years in power as Hungarian opposition wins election landslide |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c2d8zw2d3rkt |website=BBC News |access-date=15 June 2026 |archive-date=April 12, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260412231358/https://www.bbc.com/news/live/c2d8zw2d3rkt |url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[2026 Beninese presidential election]]: Independent candidate [[Romuald Wadagni]] wins in a landslide with over 94% of the vote.<ref name="ReutersWadagni">{{Cite news |title=Benin's Wadagni wins presidency in landslide with over 94% of votes |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/benins-finance-minister-wadagni-wins-presidential-election-with-94-landslide-2026-04-13/ |date=13 April 2026 |access-date=14 April 2026 |work=Reuters |lang=en |quote=Benin's Finance Minister Romuald Wadagni secured a landslide victory in the West African nation's April 12 presidential election, garnering over 94% of votes, provisional results from the electoral commission showed on Monday.}}</ref>
* [[April 13]] – [[2026 Iran war]]: A [[2026 United States naval blockade of Iran|blockade of Iranian ports]] by the United States takes effect, with President Trump warning that any Iranian vessels attempting to challenge it will be "immediately eliminated". Maritime authorities advise ships in the region to expect increased military activity and possible interception procedures.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-13 |title=US blockade of Iranian ports takes effect as Trump threatens to destroy 'attack ships' |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cp9vm5ezxz4t |access-date=2026-04-13 |website=BBC News |archive-date=May 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260514084544/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cp9vm5ezxz4t |url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[April 16]] – [[2026 Lebanon war]]: A [[US]]-brokered [[2026 Israel–Lebanon ceasefire|10-day ceasefire]] takes effect between [[Israel]] and [[Lebanon]], following ambassador-level talks in the [[White House]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-24 |title=Israeli warplanes strike southern Lebanon despite ceasefire |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/israeli-warplanes-strike-southern-lebanon-despite-ceasefire/3916985 |access-date=2026-04-25 |website=Anadolu |language=tr}}</ref>
* [[April 19]] – [[2026 Bulgarian parliamentary election]]: The [[Progressive Bulgaria]] coalition, led by former President [[Rumen Radev]], wins a landslide victory, securing 44% of the vote and an outright majority of seats.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://dariknews.bg/novini/bylgariia/cik-pri-100-obraboteni-protokoli-progresivna-bylgariia-pecheli-vota-gerb-sds-vtori-treti-sa-pp-db-2452551|title=ЦИК при 100% обработени протоколи: "Прогресивна България" печели вота, ГЕРБ-СДС втори, трети са ПП-ДБ|date=April 20, 2026|website=dariknews.bg|language=bg|access-date=April 20, 2026|archive-date=April 20, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260420132004/https://dariknews.bg/novini/bylgariia/cik-pri-100-obraboteni-protokoli-progresivna-bylgariia-pecheli-vota-gerb-sds-vtori-treti-sa-pp-db-2452551|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[April 21]] – [[2026 Iran war]]: US President Trump announces a further extension of the [[2026 Iran war ceasefire|ceasefire]] until an Iranian proposal is submitted and conversations are concluded at the request of [[Pakistan]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-21 |title=Trump says the United States is extending ⁠its ⁠ceasefire with Iran at mediator Pakistan's request to allow more time for Tehran to put forward its proposal |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/21/iran-war-live-tehran-shuns-talks-trump-says-us-blockade-to-remain |access-date=2026-04-22 |website=[[Al Jazeera English]] |language=en |archive-date=April 27, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260427025633/https://www.aljazeera.com/news/liveblog/2026/4/21/iran-war-live-tehran-shuns-talks-trump-says-us-blockade-to-remain |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[April 23]] – [[Tornado outbreak sequence of April 23–28, 2026]]: An EF4 tornado hits the [[Vance Air Force Base]] in [[Enid, Oklahoma]], injuring one person and damaging or destroying homes.
* [[April 25]] – [[2026 Mali offensives]]: The [[Azawad Liberation Front]] and [[JNIM]] launch several large-scale attacks, targeting major cities across [[Mali]], capturing [[Kidal]] and parts of [[Gao]], [[Mopti]], and [[Sevare]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/25/armed-groups-stage-simultaneous-attacks-across-mali |title=Armed groups stage simultaneous attacks across Mali |publisher=Al Jazeera |date=25 April 2026 |access-date=April 26, 2026 |archive-date=April 30, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260430171037/https://www.aljazeera.com/video/newsfeed/2026/4/25/armed-groups-stage-simultaneous-attacks-across-mali |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== May ===
[[File: Liuyang fireworks plant explosion-20260504 (8x5 crop).png|thumb|Firefighters at the scene of the [[2026 Liuyang fireworks factory explosion|Liuyang fireworks factory explosion]], which occurred on May 4]]
[[File:Flamingo_Revolution_Tirana_Protest_nr14_June_13_2026_05.jpg|thumb|Protesters in Albania's capital [[Tirana]] during the [[Flamingo Revolution]], which started on May 31]]
* [[May 1]] – The [[United Arab Emirates]] leaves [[OPEC]], ending six decades of membership and removing one of the organization's largest oil producers.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-04-30 |title=OPEC just lost one of its biggest players — here's the inside story of the UAE's exit and what the Saudi-UAE split really means for OPEC's market power |url=https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/us/opec-just-lost-one-of-its-biggest-players-heres-the-inside-story-of-the-uaes-exit-and-what-the-saudi-uae-split-really-means-for-opecs-market-power/articleshow/130634333.cms?from=mdr |access-date=2026-04-30 |website=[[The Economic Times]] |language=en |archive-date=May 1, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260501064232/https://m.economictimes.com/news/international/us/opec-just-lost-one-of-its-biggest-players-heres-the-inside-story-of-the-uaes-exit-and-what-the-saudi-uae-split-really-means-for-opecs-market-power/amp_articleshow/130634333.cms |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[May 4]]
** An [[2026 Liuyang fireworks factory explosion|explosion at a fireworks factory]] in [[Liuyang]], [[Hunan]], [[China]] kills 37 people and injures 51 others.<ref name="China fireworks:0">{{Cite web |last1=Lee |first1=Liz |last2=Bu |first2=Shi |date=8 May 2026 |editor-last=Coghill |editor-first=Kim |title=Death toll rises to 37 in China fireworks factory blast |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/china/death-toll-rises-37-china-fireworks-factory-blast-2026-05-08/ |access-date=8 May 2026 |website=Reuters}}</ref>
** [[Sudanese civil war (2023–present)|Sudanese civil war]]: [[Rapid Support Forces]] launch drone attacks at several targets in [[Khartoum]], [[Sudan]], including the [[Khartoum International Airport]] in [[Khartoum]], [[Sudan]]. Drone strikes are also reported at the Signal Corps in [[Khartoum North|Khartoum Bahri]] and Al-Markhiyat camp in northern [[Omdurman]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://sudantribune.com/article/313495|title=Drone strikes hit Khartoum airport, strategic sites as RSF escalates aerial attacks - Sudan Tribune Drone strikes hit Khartoum airport, strategic sites as RSF escalates aerial attacks|first=Omer|last=Alfarouq|date=May 4, 2026}}</ref> Additionally, the [[Sudanese Armed Forces|Sudan Army]]'s air defenses intercept drone strikes at the airport.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://yaffaps.com/en/page-99945.html|title=Sudanese Army Repels Drone Attacks Targeting Khartoum Airport; Allegations of Ethiopian Launch Site - Yaffa News Network|first=MONGID &#124; Software|last=House|website=yaffaps.com|access-date=June 15, 2026|archive-date=May 20, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520004451/https://yaffaps.com/en/page-99945.html|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[May 12]] – [[2026 Bahamian general election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Philip Davis (Bahamian politician)|Philip Davis]] wins a second term in office.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Bahamas prime minister re-elected in early election victory |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/bahamas-prime-minister-re-elected-early-election-victory-2026-05-13/ |date=13 May 2026 |access-date=13 May 2026 |work=Reuters |language=en |quote=Bahamian Prime Minister Philip Davis and his ruling ‌Progressive Liberal Party were re-elected on Tuesday, making him the first leader to be elected ⁠to a second consecutive term in nearly 30 years.}}</ref>
* [[May 12]]{{ndash}}[[May 16|16]] – The [[Eurovision Song Contest 2026]] is held in [[Vienna]], Austria, following [[Austria in the Eurovision Song Contest|their win]] at the [[Eurovision Song Contest 2025]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Schumacher|first=Elizabeth|title=Eurovision: Vienna to host European Song Contest 2026|url=https://www.dw.com/en/eurovision-vienna-to-host-european-song-contest-2026/a-73697370|publisher=Deutsche Welle|access-date=22 August 2025|archive-date=August 22, 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250822033113/https://www.dw.com/en/eurovision-vienna-to-host-european-song-contest-2026/a-73697370|url-status=live}}</ref> Bulgarian contestant [[Dara (Bulgarian singer)|Dara]] wins with the song "[[Bangaranga]]", marking the first time [[Bulgaria in the Eurovision Song Contest|Bulgaria]] has won the contest.<ref>{{Cite news |date=16 May 2026 |title=Bulgaria wins Eurovision Song Contest, Israel comes second again |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/eurovision-song-contest-final-takes-stage-amid-gaza-boycott-2026-05-16/ |access-date=17 May 2026 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[May 15]] – [[Gaza war]]: An Israeli strike assassinates [[Izz al-Din al-Haddad]], commander of the Izz al-Din al-Qassam Brigades and leader of [[Hamas]] in the Gaza Strip.<ref>{{Cite news |date=16 May 2026 |title=Israel's military says Hamas armed chief killed in air strike on Gaza |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/gaza-mosques-announce-death-hamas-military-leader-after-israeli-targeting-claim-2026-05-16/ |access-date=16 May 2026 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[May 16]] – [[2026 Ituri Province Ebola epidemic]]: The [[World Health Organization]] declares an [[Ebola]] outbreak caused by ''[[Bundibugyo ebolavirus]]'' in the [[Democratic Republic of the Congo]] and [[Uganda]] a [[Public Health Emergency of International Concern]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=17 May 2026 |title=Epidemic of Ebola Disease caused by Bundibugyo virus in the Democratic Republic of the Congo and Uganda determined a public health emergency of international concern |url=https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern |access-date=17 May 2026 |website=[[World Health Organization]] |archive-date=May 20, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260520044450/https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last1=Mishra |first1=Disha |last2=Khushi |first2=Akanksha |date=17 May 2026 |title=WHO declares Ebola outbreak in Congo, Uganda an emergency of international concern |url=https://www.reuters.com/business/healthcare-pharmaceuticals/who-declares-ebola-outbreak-congo-uganda-global-health-emergency-2026-05-17/ |access-date=17 May 2026 |work=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[May 17]] – [[2026 Cape Verdean parliamentary election]]: Incumbent Prime Minister [[Ulisses Correia e Silva]] loses reelection to [[African Party for the Independence of Cape Verde|PAICV]] leader [[Francisco Carvalho]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-02-12 |title=The electoral calendar for the 2026 legislative elections is now available. (English translation) |url=https://cne.cv/sala_de_imprensa_/calendario-eleitoral-das-eleicoes-legislativas-2026-ja-disponivel/ |access-date=2026-03-02 |website=Comissão Nacional de Eleições (CNE) }}</ref>
* [[May 20]] – Former [[First Secretary of the Communist Party of Cuba]] [[Raúl Castro]] is indicted by the [[United States]] over the [[1996 shootdown of Brothers to the Rescue aircraft]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-20 |title=US charges Cuba's Raúl Castro with murder over 1996 downing of two planes |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c3r219yxl5eo |access-date=2026-05-21 |website=BBC |language=en}}</ref>
* [[May 22]]
** The [[2026 European heatwaves]] begin, bringing record-breaking temperatures to several European countries and causing thousands of deaths over the next several weeks.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Lawless |first=Jill |date=26 May 2026 |title=Exceptionally early heat wave shatters records and brings deaths in Europe |url=https://apnews.com/article/europe-heatwave-temperature-records-france-uk-5e08af7830e72ffa9fccdcf48cf4f7b5 |access-date=30 May 2026 |work=Associated Press |archive-date=May 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260528172703/https://apnews.com/article/europe-heatwave-temperature-records-france-uk-5e08af7830e72ffa9fccdcf48cf4f7b5 |url-status=live }}</ref>
** A [[2026 Liushenyu coal mine explosion|gas explosion at the Liushenyu coal mine]] in [[Shanxi]], China, kills 82 people.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-05-23 |title=At least 82 killed in Chinese coal mine explosion |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5y0ve18qlko |access-date=2026-05-23 |website=BBC News |language=en |archive-date=May 23, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260523212406/https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5y0ve18qlko |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[May 24]] – [[2026 Cypriot legislative election]]: The [[Democratic Rally]] led by [[Annita Demetriou]] wins a plurality of seats.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2025-05-20 |title=Parliamentary elections set for May 24 next year |url=https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/05/20/parliamentary-elections-set-for-may-24-next-year |access-date=2025-11-08 |website=cyprus-mail.com |language=en |archive-date=January 16, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260116185359/https://cyprus-mail.com/2025/05/20/parliamentary-elections-set-for-may-24-next-year |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[May 30]] – [[2026 Maltese general election]]: The [[Labour Party (Malta)|Labour Party]] led by incumbent Prime Minister [[Robert Abela]] wins their fourth consecutive election.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Borg |first=Neville |date=2026-04-27 |title=Robert Abela announces snap election for May 30 |url=https://timesofmalta.com/article/abela-announces-election-date.1126985 |access-date=2026-04-27 |website=Times of Malta |language=en-gb |archive-date=April 28, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260428043726/https://timesofmalta.com/article/abela-announces-election-date.1126985 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[May 31]]
** [[2026 Guinean parliamentary election]]: Parties supporting incumbent President [[Mamady Doumbouya]] win the election.<ref>{{cite web |website=Le360Afrique |date=22 February 2026 |title= Guinée: les élections législatives et communales prévues le 24 mai
|url=https://afrique.le360.ma/politique/guinee-les-elections-legislatives-et-communales-prevues-le-24-mai_LPQ3R2EQ3NHY7G26CB5CPJB5CU/|access-date=14 March 2026|language=fr}}</ref>
** [[Flamingo Revolution]]: Following small protests in the village of [[Zvërnec]], major protests erupt in [[Albania]] over a proposed luxury development involving [[Donald Trump]]'s son-in-law [[Jared Kushner]] and his firm [[Affinity Partners]], as well as broader discontent with Prime Minister [[Edi Rama]]'s government.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Protests against luxury resort in Albania linked to Jared Kushner now in second day |last=Flori |first=Anna |date=June 2, 2026 |url=https://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2026/06/02/protests-against-luxury-resort-in-albania-linked-to-jared-jushner-now-in-second-day |access-date=June 5, 2026 |website=www.euronews.com |archive-date=June 3, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260603182454/https://www.euronews.com/my-europe/2026/06/02/protests-against-luxury-resort-in-albania-linked-to-jared-jushner-now-in-second-day |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== June ===
