* [[June 1]] – [[2026 Ethiopian general election]]: The [[Prosperity Party]], led by incumbent Prime Minister [[Abiy Ahmed]], wins reelection.<ref>{{Cite news|title=National Election Board Says Most Constituencies Declared Election Results|url=https://www.ena.et/web/eng/w/eng_8993217|access-date=June 6, 2026|language=en|agency= Ethiopian News Agency}}</ref>
* [[June 6]] – [[2026 Delhi Jantar Mantar protests]]: A series of demonstrations takes place in [[Jantar Mantar, New Delhi]], initiated by the [[Cockroach Janta Party]], an Indian youth-based [[Political satire|satirical political movement]], along with other student organisations.<ref>{{Cite web |first=Yashraj |last=Sharma |date=6 June 2026 |title=I'm a cockroach': Gen Z protest movement lands in Indian capital |url=https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/6/6/im-a-cockroach-gen-z-protest-movement-lands-in-indian-capital |website=[[Al Jazeera English]] |access-date=22 July 2026 |archive-date=10 June 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260610204831/https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/6/6/im-a-cockroach-gen-z-protest-movement-lands-in-indian-capital |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 7]] 
** [[2026 Armenian parliamentary election]]: The [[Civil Contract (Armenia)|Civil Contract]], led by incumbent Prime Minister [[Nikol Pashinyan]], wins reelection.<ref>{{cite web |last1=DEMOURIAN |first1=AVET |title=Armenian Prime Minister Pashinyan claims victory in election seen as test of Russia's influence |url=https://apnews.com/article/armenia-election-pashinyan-6e73e44ff1fea62aecf20c8d7bfabe2c |website=[[Associated Press]] |date=June 8, 2026 |access-date=10 June 2026}}</ref>
** [[2026 Kosovan parliamentary election]]: Amid the ongoing [[2025–2026 Kosovo political deadlock|political deadlock]], [[Vetëvendosje]], led by incumbent Prime Minister [[Albin Kurti]], wins a plurality of seats.<ref>{{cite news |date=28 April 2026 |title=Kosovo heads to elections after failure to elect president |url=https://www.koha.net/en/arberi/kosova-shkon-ne-zgjedhje-pas-deshtimit-per-president |access-date=21 April 2026 |work=Koha }}{{Dead link|date=July 2026 |bot=InternetArchiveBot }}</ref>{{update-inline|date=June 2026}}
** [[2026 Peruvian general election]]: [[Popular Force]] leader [[Keiko Fujimori]] narrowly defeats [[Together for Peru]] leader [[Roberto Sánchez (Peruvian politician)|Roberto Sánchez]] in the presidential runoff. Left-wing parties gain a majority in the [[Chamber of Deputies (Peru)|Chamber of Deputies]] but tie in the reestablished [[Senate of Peru|Senate]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 June 2026 |title=Keiko Fujimori's expected victory returns divisive dynasty to Peru |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/americas/keiko-fujimoris-expected-victory-returns-divisive-dynasty-peru-2026-06-24/ |access-date=24 June 2026 |website=Reuters |language=en}}</ref>
* [[June 8]] – A powerful [[2026 Mindanao earthquake|magnitude 7.8 earthquake]] strikes the Philippines, the strongest in the country since 1976. 107 are killed and 1,319 are injured.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Magramo |first=Kathleen |date=2026-06-08 |title=7.8 magnitude earthquake hits southern Philippines |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/06/07/asia/southern-philippines-mindanao-earthquake-intl-hnk |access-date=2026-06-08 |website=CNN |language=en}}</ref>
* [[June 9]] – Turkey and [[Saudi Arabia]] sign an agreement to revive the 19th century [[Hejaz railway]].<ref>{{cite news |title=How the Hejaz railway could reshape Middle East geopolitics |url=https://www.trtworld.com/article/6633f6e591db |access-date=21 July 2026 |work=[[TRT World]] |date=June 26, 2026 |language=en}}</ref>
* [[June 10]] – In [[Barcelona]], Spain, the blessing ceremony of the [[Sagrada Família]]'s tallest tower by [[Pope Leo XIV]] is held, exactly 100 years after the death of architect [[Antoni Gaudí]]. Pope Leo XIV consecrates and opens the central tower of Jesus Christ.<ref>{{cite news |title=Crowds turn out in Barcelona for pope blessing Sagrada Família's final tower |url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jun/10/pope-leo-bless-sagrada-familia-antoni-gaudi |work=The Guardian |date=10 June 2026 |access-date=12 June 2026}}</ref> The Sagrada Família is [[List of tallest church buildings|the world's tallest church]].<ref>{{cite news |last=Henriques |first=Martha |date=9 June 2026 |title='A place of legend': The ancient engineering marvels of the world's tallest church |url=https://www.bbc.com/future/article/20260608-sagrada-famlia-the-ancient-engineering-marvels-of-the-worlds-tallest-church |publisher=British Broadcasting Corporation |access-date=25 June 2026}}</ref>
* [[June 11]] – The [[National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration]] declares the onset of an [[El Niño]] event in the tropical Pacific, and forecasts a 63% chance that it will rank among the largest since records began in 1950.<ref>{{cite news |title=El Niño under way and threatens weather extremes, scientists say |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c75ylx7g00xo |work=BBC News |date=11 June 2026 |access-date=11 June 2026}}</ref>
* [[June 11]] – [[July 19]] – The [[2026 FIFA World Cup]] is held in [[Canada]], [[Mexico]], and the [[United States]], and is won by [[Spain national football team|Spain]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-07-19 |title=Spain wins 2026 FIFA World Cup with grueling 1-0 win over Argentina - CBS News |url=https://www.cbsnews.com/news/2026-fifa-world-cup-final-spain-argentina-sunday/ |access-date=2026-07-19 |website=www.cbsnews.com |language=en-US}}</ref>
* [[June 12]] – [[Elon Musk]] becomes the first US dollar [[trillionaire]] with the [[initial public offering of SpaceX]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-today-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-05-20-2026 |title=SpaceX Filing Starts Countdown to Massive IPO |date=May 20, 2026 |work=[[The Wall Street Journal]] |access-date=May 27, 2026 |archive-date=May 27, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260527051217/https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/stock-market-today-dow-sp-500-nasdaq-05-20-2026 |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 12]] – [[July 5]] – The [[2026 Women's T20 World Cup]] is held in [[England]] and [[Wales]], and [[2026 Women's T20 World Cup final|is won]] by [[Australia women's national cricket team|Australia]].<ref>{{cite web |access-date=5 July 2026 |title=Invincible Australia crowned Women's T20WC champions |url=https://www.icc-cricket.com/tournaments/womens-t20-worldcup-2026/news/england-australia-final-womens-t20-world-cup-2026 |website=International Cricket Council |date=July 5, 2026 |language=en}}</ref>
* [[June 13]]–[[June 14|14]] – The [[2026 24 Hours of Le Mans]] is held in [[Le Mans]], France.<ref>{{Cite web |title=The Headlines After 12 Hours at Le Mans |url= https://www.fiawec.com/en/news/the-headlines-after-12-hours-at-le-mans/13629 |access-date=2026-06-14 |website=fiawec.com |language=en}}</ref>
* [[June 14]] – [[2026 Rio de Janeiro mid-air collision|A mid-air collision between two helicopters]] in [[Rio de Janeiro]], Brazil, kills six people, including American singer-songwriter [[Oliver Tree]], Argentine YouTuber [[Gaspi]], Argentine director and screenwriter [[Lucas A. Vignale]] and Brazilian music producer [[Lucas Frota]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-14 |title=Acidente de helicóptero no Rio: Oliver Tree e Gaspi entre vítimas |url=https://g1.globo.com/rj/rio-de-janeiro/noticia/2026/06/14/youtuber-argentino-gaspi-e-cantor-americano-oliver-tree-estao-entre-as-vitimas-de-acidente-de-helicoptero-no-rio-veja-lista.ghtml |access-date=2026-06-14 |website=G1 |language=pt-BR}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-14 |title=Cantor Oliver Tree é um dos mortos em acidente aéreo no Rio; veja vítimas |url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/nacional/sudeste/rj/cantor-oliver-tree-e-um-dos-mortos-em-acidente-aereo-no-rio-veja-vitimas/ |access-date=2026-06-14 |website=CNN Brasil |language=pt-BR |archive-date=June 14, 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260614183128/https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/nacional/sudeste/rj/cantor-oliver-tree-e-um-dos-mortos-em-acidente-aereo-no-rio-veja-vitimas/ |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[June 15]]–[[June 17|17]] – The [[United States]] and [[Iran]] announce and sign the [[Islamabad Memorandum]], a 14-point agreement to end the [[2026 Iran war]], reopen the [[Strait of Hormuz]], lift the U.S. blockade of Iranian ports, and begin a 60-day negotiation period on Iran's nuclear programme; [[Israel]] says it will not withdraw from [[Israeli occupation of Southern Lebanon (2026)|territory it has seized]] in southern [[Lebanon]].<ref>{{cite news |last1=Hafezi |first1=Parisa |last2=Stewart |first2=Phil |last3=Ehab |first3=Yomna |title=US, Iran reach preliminary agreement to end war, signing set for Friday |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/us-iran-reach-peace-deal-signing-set-friday-pakistan-says-2026-06-14/ |work=Reuters |date=15 June 2026 |access-date=15 June 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Holland |first1=Steve |last2=Hafezi |first2=Parisa |last3=Ehab |first3=Yomna |title=US and Iran presidents sign ceasefire agreement, but Trump says he could still resume attacks |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/g7-leaders-demand-ceasefire-lebanon-welcome-iran-deal-2026-06-17/ |work=Reuters |date=18 June 2026 |access-date=20 June 2026}}</ref>
* [[June 21]] – [[2026 Colombian presidential election]]: Right-wing outsider [[Abelardo de la Espriella]] wins the election in a runoff against left-wing candidate [[Iván Cepeda]].<ref>{{Cite news |last1=Garcia Cano |first1=Regina |last2=Suarez |first2=Astrid |date=25 June 2026 |title=Trump-endorsed de la Espriella declared winner of Colombia's presidential runoff election |url=https://apnews.com/article/colombia-election-ivan-cepeda-concedes-de-la-espriella-e0a39ed59a9d432d318e11c1e0735f4e |work=AP News}}</ref>
* [[June 22]] – [[Keir Starmer]] announces his resignation as [[Prime Minister of the United Kingdom]], prompting a [[2026 Labour Party leadership election (UK)|leadership election]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Wheeler |first=Richard |date=2026-06-22 |title=Keir Starmer announces resignation as prime minister and Labour Party leader |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cdxd00lg599o |access-date=2026-06-22 |website=BBC |language=en-GB}}</ref>
* [[June 24]] – [[2026 Venezuela earthquakes|Two consecutive earthquakes]] with magnitudes of {{M|w|link=y|7.2}}, and {{M|w|7.5}} shake western Venezuela. At least 6,300 people are killed, with thousands injured or missing and widespread damage across the country.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Janetsky |first1=Megan |last2=Rincón |first2=Andry |last3=Arraez |first3=Juan Pablo |date=2026-06-26 |title=Neighbors dig through Venezuela rubble to search for loved ones as death toll climbs |url=https://apnews.com/article/venezuela-caracas-guaira-earthquakes-dead-injured-missing-b07aff1cb886cfe616a0e89b3687b8b8 |access-date=2026-06-26 |website=AP News |language=en}}</ref>

