* [[July 4]]–[[July 18|18]] – The [[2026 Nations Championship|inaugural]] [[Nations Championship]] – [[2026 Nations Championship Southern Hemisphere Series|Southern Hemisphere Series]], an international rugby union tournament, is held.<ref name="nations_championship">{{Cite web|url=https://nationschampionshiprugby.com/en|title=Nations Championship}}</ref>
* [[July 6]] – [[Hamas]] announces the [[Gaza Strip under Hamas|resignation of its civil administration]] under the [[Gaza peace plan]].<ref>{{#invoke:cite|web|url=https://www.haaretz.com/israel-news/israel-security/2026-07-06/ty-article-live/israeli-civilians-tried-to-cross-into-syria-idf-says-amid-settlement-reports/0000019f-342c-d746-adff-ff6d69240000?liveBlogItemId=920670504#920670504|title= Hamas says group-backed Gaza government resigns to hand power to Palestinian technocrats|website=[[Haaretz]]|date=6 July 2026}}</ref>
* [[July 7]] – The [[International Olympic Committee]] lifts the ban on the [[Russian Olympic Committee]], allowing its athletes to participate in future Olympic Games.<ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-07-07 |title=IOC provisionally lifts suspension of Russian Olympic Committee – Recommendations to IFs with regard to Russian athletes' participation no longer applicable |url=https://www.olympics.com/ioc/news/ioc-provisionally-lifts-suspension-of-russian-olympic-committee-recommendations-to-ifs-with-regard-to-russian-athletes-participation-no-longer-applicable |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260726212518/https://www.olympics.com/ioc/news/ioc-provisionally-lifts-suspension-of-russian-olympic-committee-recommendations-to-ifs-with-regard-to-russian-athletes-participation-no-longer-applicable |archive-date=July 26, 2026 |access-date=2026-08-04 |work=Olympics.com |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref>
* [[July 7]]–[[July 8|8]] – The [[2026 Ankara NATO summit|2026 NATO summit]] is held in [[Ankara]], [[Turkey]].<ref>{{cite web |title=NATO Summit 2026 |url=https://www.nato.int/en/news-and-events/events/event-programmes/2026/07/nato-summit-2026 |website=NATO |date=7 July 2026 |access-date=7 July 2026}}</ref>
* [[July 8]] – [[2026 Iran war]]: The [[Islamabad Memorandum]] between the [[United States]] and [[Iran]] breaks down, with U.S. President Trump saying the agreement is "over" following renewed U.S. strikes on Iranian targets.<ref>{{cite news |title=Trump says interim accord with Iran to end war is "over" |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/trump-says-interim-accord-with-iran-end-war-is-over-2026-07-08/ |work=Reuters |date=8 July 2026 |access-date=8 July 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=US says it has completed a new round of strikes on Iran |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-says-it-has-completed-a-new-round-strikes-iran-2026-07-08/ |work=Reuters |date=8 July 2026 |access-date=8 July 2026}}</ref>
* [[July 12]]–[[July 13|13]] – [[2026 Bangkok pub fire|A fire at the Rong Beer Na Lat Phrao live-music venue]] in [[Chatuchak district]], [[Bangkok]], kills 34 people and injures more than 70 others.<ref name="Bangkok_Post">{{cite news |date=16 July 2026 |title=Singer's death brings Bangkok pub fire toll to 33 |url=https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/general/3286820/singers-death-brings-bangkok-pub-fire-toll-to-33 |access-date=16 July 2026 |work=[[Bangkok Post]] |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260717162133/https://www.bangkokpost.com/thailand/general/3286820/singers-death-brings-bangkok-pub-fire-toll-to-33 |archive-date=17 July 2026}}</ref>
* [[July 18]] – The [[Mile run world record progression|world record]] for the [[mile run]] is broken by British runner [[Josh Kerr (runner)|Josh Kerr]] at the [[London Athletics Meet]], with a time of 3:42.66 surpassing the previous record held by [[Hicham El Guerrouj]] since 1999.<ref>{{cite news |title=Britain's Kerr breaks 27-year mile world record in London |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/athletics/articles/cx2jl1wge2po |work=BBC Sport |date=18 July 2026 |access-date=18 July 2026}}</ref>
