** [[2026 São Toméan presidential election]]: Incumbent President [[Carlos Vila Nova]] is reelected for a second term.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Sao Tome Presidential Election, 2026 |url=https://www.poliglobe.com/election/1307 |website=Poliglobe |access-date=January 23, 2026 |archive-date=December 19, 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251219051151/https://www.poliglobe.com/election/1307 |url-status=live }}</ref>
** [[2026 FIFA World Cup final]]: [[Spain national football team|Spain]] beat defending champions [[Argentina national football team|Argentina]] 1–0 during [[Overtime (sports)#Association football|extra time]] to win a second [[FIFA World Cup]] title after 16 years. Spanish forward [[Ferran Torres]] scores the only goal in the 106th minute.<ref>{{cite news |title=Spain wins the World Cup by beating Argentina 1-0 on Ferran Torres' goal in extra time |url=https://apnews.com/article/fccc26aa12d9226e63d06b601b770617 |work=Associated Press |date=19 July 2026 |access-date=19 July 2026}}</ref>
* [[July 20]]
** [[Andy Burnham]] is appointed by King [[Charles III]] as [[Prime Minister of the United Kingdom]], succeeding [[Keir Starmer]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Andy Burnham pledges cost of living help in first speech as prime minister |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/live/cgrkv8e8l9qt |work=BBC News |date=20 July 2026 |access-date=20 July 2026}}</ref>
** [[2026 Iran war]]: The [[Houthis]] announce a maritime [[Houthi blockade of Saudi Arabia|blockade]] against Saudi Arabia on the [[Bab-el-Mandeb|Bab el-Mandeb]] strait.<ref>{{cite news |title=Yemen's Houthis declare naval blockade against Saudi Arabia |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/yemens-houthis-declare-naval-blockade-against-saudi-arabia-statement-2026-07-20/ |access-date=21 July 2026 |work=Reuters |date=July 20, 2026}}</ref>
