* [[August 12]] – A [[Solar eclipse of August 12, 2026|total solar eclipse]] occurs in parts of Europe, the first in continental Europe since [[Solar eclipse of August 11, 1999|1999]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dobrijevic |first=Daisy |date=August 5, 2026 |title=Total solar eclipse Aug. 12, 2026 live updates |url=https://www.space.com/news/live/total-solar-eclipse-today-aug-12-2026-live-updates |access-date=August 14, 2026 |website=[[Space.com]] |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Korosec |first=Marko |date=August 11, 2026 |title=Total Solar Eclipse Targets Europe: First Path of Totality in 27 Years Arrives August 12 |url=https://www.severe-weather.eu/global-weather/total-solar-eclipse-spain-iceland-europe-august-12th-2026-mk/ |access-date=August 14, 2026 |website=Severe Weather Europe}}</ref>
* [[August 13]] – [[2026 Zambian general election]]: Incumbent President [[Hakainde Hichilema]] wins reelection, and the [[United Party for National Development|UPND]] wins a majority in the [[National Assembly of Zambia|National Assembly]].<ref>{{Cite web|title=Zambia invites EU as observer to 2026 general elections|url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/africa/zambia-invites-eu-as-observer-to-2026-general-elections/3575445|website=aa.com.tr|access-date=2025-11-28|date=2025-05-21|archive-date=May 18, 2026|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260518221837/https://www.aa.com.tr/en/africa/zambia-invites-eu-as-observer-to-2026-general-elections/3575445|url-status=live}}</ref>
* [[August 15]] – At least 136 people are killed and nearly 1,300 injured when a [[2026 Flores earthquake|magnitude 7.7 earthquake]] strikes off the island of [[Flores]], [[Indonesia]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-08-15 |title=Powerful 7.7-magnitude earthquake kills at least 38 in Indonesia|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c5y0zz63gero |access-date=2026-08-15 |website=BBC News}}</ref>
* [[August 18]] – [[2026 Zamboye mine collapse]]: More than 100 people are killed in a landslide at an [[Artisanal mining|artisanal]] [[gold mining]] site in [[Zamboye]], [[Nana-Mambéré]], [[Central African Republic]], near the [[Cameroon–Central African Republic border|border with Cameroon]].<ref>{{Cite news |last=Njie |first=Paul |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cly9dwe5pzeo |title=Gold mine hit by deadly landslide in CAR near border with Cameroon |work=BBC News |date=19 August 2026 |access-date=23 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/africa/landslide-gold-mining-site-central-african-republic-kills-over-100-mining-group-2026-08-19/ |title=Central African Republic artisanal gold mine collapses, killing more than 100 |work=Reuters |date=19 August 2026 |access-date=23 August 2026}}</ref>
* [[August 20]]
** [[2026 Iran war]]: [[President of the United States|U.S. President]] [[Donald Trump]] announces an "[[Economic D-Day]]" against [[Iran]], calling on allies to join efforts to isolate Iran economically.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Saikal |first=Amin |editor-first1=Justin |editor-last1=Bergman |date=2026-09-01 |title=Sanctions and bombs won't end the war in Iran. Trump is running out of options against an intractable foe |url=https://doi.org/10.64628/aa.rh9etjgpa |access-date=2026-09-14 |website=doi.org |doi=10.64628/aa.rh9etjgpa |url-access=subscription }}</ref> 
** [[Rojava Revolution]]: The [[Syrian Democratic Forces]] announces its integration into the [[Syrian Army]], resulting in the dissolution of the [[Democratic Autonomous Administration of North and East Syria]] in favor of the [[Syrian transitional government|Syrian government]] under [[Ahmed al-Sharaa]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Morris-Gray |first=Eve |date=2026-08-25 |title=SDF Dissolves as Kurdish Leaders move into Syrian State |url=https://theamargi.com/posts/sdf-dissolves-as-kurdish-leaders-move-into-syrian-state |access-date=2026-08-25 |website=The Amargi |language=en}}</ref> 
* [[August 23]] – [[2026 Kazakh legislative election]]: Pro-[[Tokayev]] party [[Ädilet (political party)|Ädilet]] wins a [[supermajority]] in the newly established [[Kurultai (Kazakhstan)|Kurultai]].<ref name="Reut2">{{cite web |date=1 July 2026 |title=Kazakhstan to hold snap parliamentary election on August 23 |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/kazakhstan-hold-snap-parliamentary-election-august-23-2026-07-01/ |access-date=2 July 2026 |website=Reuters}}</ref>
* [[August 24]] – [[Aftermath of the Syrian civil war]]: The US removes Syria and [[Hay'at Tahrir al-Sham]] from its list of designated [[US-designated state sponsors of terrorism|state sponsors of terrorism]], lifting restrictions on foreign investments in the country and allowing services like [[VISA]] to work in Syria.<ref name="sharaaVisaCard" /><ref>{{cite news |title=US removes Syria from terrorism sponsor list, lifting major investment obstacle |url=https://www.reuters.com/world/middle-east/us-removes-syrias-designation-state-sponsor-terrorism-2026-08-24/ |access-date=27 August 2026 |work=Reuters |date=August 25, 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |last1=Abdulrahim |first1=Raja |title=U.S. Removes Syria From Its List of Terrorism Sponsors |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2026/08/25/world/middleeast/us-syria-terrorism-list-sanctions.html |access-date=27 August 2026 |work=The New York Times |date=25 August 2026}}</ref> Syria has been on the list since 1979.<ref name="sharaaVisaCard">{{cite news |title=Syrian president makes landmark Visa card payment |url=https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/syrian-president-makes-landmark-visa-card-payment/4038705 |access-date=27 August 2026 |work=Anadolu Agency |date=27 August 2026 |language=tr}}</ref>
* [[August 26]]
** At least 12 are killed and 56 injured, when over 150 [[Wildfire|wildfires]] break out in [[Algeria]], prompting calls from the [[Abdelmadjid Tebboune|president]] to reintroduce [[capital punishment]] for convicted arsonists, which has not been practiced in the country since 1993.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Digital |first=N. H. |date=2026-08-27 |title=12 killed, 54 injured as wildfires ravage northeastern Algeria |url=https://www.nationalheraldindia.com/international/algeria-battles-deadly-wildfires-as-heatwave-fuels-flames-across-the-northeast |access-date=2026-09-17 |website=National Herald |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=2026-09-03 |title=Algerians battle deadly wildfires as Tebboune seeks death penalty for arson |url=https://apnews.com/article/algeria-wildfires-death-penalty-tebboune-93becdb9d2da981480e7f4a4113879ec |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260905212515/https://apnews.com/article/algeria-wildfires-death-penalty-tebboune-93becdb9d2da981480e7f4a4113879ec |archive-date=September 5, 2026 |access-date=2026-09-17 |work=AP News |language=en |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-09-01 |title=Algeria forest fires: President Abdelmadjid Tebboune seeks death penalty for arsonists |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgy41lwe0jo |access-date=2026-09-17 |website=www.bbc.com |language=en-GB}}</ref>
** [[2026 Nepal–Tibet floods]]: At least 1,403 people are killed and 6,650 are reported missing after a [[landslide]] and [[Glacier collapse|glacial collapse]] trigger [[Flash flood|flash floods]] and [[Debris flow|debris flows]] at the border between [[Nepal]] and the [[Tibet Autonomous Region]] of China.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Nepal flood death toll crosses 1,400; over 6,000 still missing|url=https://www.msn.com/en-in/news/other/nepal-flood-death-toll-crosses-1400-over-6000-still-missing/ar-AA2clZZm |access-date=2026-09-17 |website=www.msn.com}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web|title=What caused Nepal flood? Scientist says it was enormous landslide, glacier fall |url=https://abcnews.com/International/deadly-nepal-flood-caused-enormous-landslide-glacier-tumble/story?id=135984405 |access-date=2026-09-17 |website=ABC News |language=en}}</ref>
* [[August 28]] – King [[Harald V]] of Norway [[Death and state funeral of Harald V|dies]] and is succeeded by his son, King [[Haakon VIII]].<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Doherty |first1=Caitlin |last2=Yeung |first2=Tinshui |date=2026-08-28 |title=King Haakon VIII takes the throne in Norway following death of Harald V - follow live |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/live/cm36lpzwglrwt |access-date=2026-08-28 |website=BBC News |language=en-GB}}</ref>
* [[August 29]]
** [[2026 Icelandic European Union membership negotiations referendum]]: A referendum to continue negotiations for [[Iceland]] to join the [[European Union]] is rejected.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Euractiv |date=2026-03-06 |title=Iceland locks in on date for EU referendum |url=https://www.euractiv.com/news/iceland-locks-in-on-date-for-eu-referendum/ |access-date=2026-08-11 |website=Euractiv |language=en-GB}}</ref>
** [[2026 Nigerien coup attempt]]: A [[mutiny|mutinous]] faction of the [[Niger Armed Forces]] called the Armed Forces for the Restoration of the Fatherland attempt a coup against president [[Abdourahamane Tiani]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Niger junta says it is back in control after attempted coup |url=https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/08/30/niger-junta-says-it-is-back-in-control-after-attempted-coup_6756980_4.html |access-date=1 September 2026 |work=[[Le Monde]] |date=30 August 2026}}</ref>
** [[Jiang (rank)|''Daejang'']] (대장) [[Kim Song-gi]] becomes the new [[Ministry of National Defence (North Korea)|Minister of]] [[Ministry of National Defence (North Korea)|National Defence]] of the [[Korean People's Army]] (replacing [[No Kwang-chol]]).
* [[August 30]] – [[NASA]] launches the flagship [[Nancy Grace Roman Space Telescope]] aboard a [[SpaceX]] [[Falcon Heavy]] rocket. Designed to study [[dark energy]], [[dark matter]] and [[exoplanet]]s, the observatory has a field of view at least 100 times larger than the [[Hubble Space Telescope]]'s.<ref>{{cite news |title=NASA launches powerful new Roman Space Telescope from Florida |url=https://www.reuters.com/science/nasa-launches-powerful-new-roman-space-telescope-florida-2026-08-30/ |work=[[Reuters]] |date=30 August 2026 |access-date=30 August 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Why the Roman Space Telescope? |date=October 24, 2023 |url=https://science.nasa.gov/mission/roman-space-telescope/why-the-roman-space-telescope/ |publisher=[[NASA]] |access-date=30 August 2026}}</ref>

