== Nobel Prizes ==
[[File:Nobel medal.png|right|120px|Nobel medal]]
* [[Nobel Prize in Chemistry|Chemistry]] – [[Henri B. Kagan]] and [[Kensō Soai]], for the discovery of non-linear effects and [[autocatalysis]] in asymmetric [[organic synthesis]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 7, 2026 |title=Nobel Prize in Chemistry 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/chemistry/2026/summary/ |access-date=October 7, 2026 |website=[[Nobel Prize|The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Memorial Prize in Economic Sciences|Economics]] – [[Robert Hall (economist)|Robert E. Hall]] and [[Michael Dean Woodford|Michael Woodford]], for microeconomic foundations of [[Macroeconomic stabilization|macroeconomic stabilisation]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 12, 2026 |title=Sveriges Riksbank Prize in Economic Sciences in Memory of Alfred Nobel 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/economic-sciences/2026/summary/ |access-date=October 12, 2026 |website=[[Nobel Prize|The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Prize in Literature|Literature]] – [[Anne Carson]], for her bold and inventive [[Complete works|oeuvre]] that, in playful dialogue with the classical tradition, has created new forms for [[contemporary literature]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 8, 2026 |title=Nobel Prize in Literature 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/literature/2026/summary/ |access-date=October 8, 2026 |website=[[Nobel Prize|The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Peace Prize|Peace]] – [[Navi Pillay]], for her efforts to promote peace and [[international law]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 9, 2026 |title=Nobel Peace Prize 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/peace/2026/summary/ |access-date=October 9, 2026 |website=[[Nobel Prize|The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Prize in Physics|Physics]] – [[Francis Halzen]], for decisive contributions to the [[IceCube Neutrino Observatory]] and the discovery of high-energy [[Neutrino|neutrinos]] of astrophysical origin.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 6, 2026 |title=Nobel Prize in Physics 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/physics/2026/summary/ |access-date=October 6, 2026 |website=[[Nobel Prize|The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>
* [[Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine|Physiology or Medicine]] – [[Karl Deisseroth]], [[Peter Hegemann]] and [[Georg Nagel]], for their discoveries concerning [[Light-gated ion channel|light-gated ion channels]] and [[optogenetics]].<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 5, 2026 |title=Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine 2026 |url=https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/2026/summary/ |access-date=October 5, 2026 |website=[[Nobel Prize|The Nobel Prize]]}}</ref>

